---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Illustration from "../components/Illustration.astro";
import selfPortrait from "../assets/self-portrait.jpeg";
import { NOW, SOCIAL } from "../config";
---
<BaseLayout title="About" active="about">
  <div class="column wrap">
    <div class="col">
      <h1>Hi, I'm Seidel, and this is my workshop.</h1>
      <p>
        I'm a Brazilian AI engineer and researcher, and I've been working in tech for over
        five years. My experience is mostly in applied AI: training, validating, and building
        robust inference pipelines for real-world applications in NLP and voice processing.
        Throughout my career I've also worked with electronics, embedded systems programming,
        and more "traditional" data science.
      </p>
      <p>
        I created this blog as open documentation of my studies and personal projects.
        Here you'll find posts and projects mostly — but not exclusively — related to my
        current work: fine-tuning, harnesses, inference setups, agentic AI, and voice processing.
        Most of what I learn ends up here as a post, and most of what I finish ends up as a
        subdomain on the projects shelf. Hopefully I'll manage a new post every week or two,
        and a new project every two or three months.
      </p>
      <p>
        While I don't intend to make any money from this blog, the shop framing is a
        joke I decided to take seriously. A robot outfitter on a distant planet, selling
        retrofits to passing ships, is a fair description of what I want this work to feel
        like: someone arrives with a vehicle, the vehicle needs a part it does not have yet, and
        the interesting problem is the fitting.
      </p>
      <p>
        Everything here is written, revised, and published by me in a very simple setup, with
        no tracking and no newsletter popup. I do use AI tools for coding and writing, but the
        ideas and opinions are my own. If something here is wrong, mail me and I'll fix it in
        public.
      </p>

      <div class="now">
        <p class="now-label">Right now</p>
        <ul>
          {NOW.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <aside class="side">
      <Illustration
        src={selfPortrait}
        alt="Cartoon portrait of Seidel, bearded and wearing a utility vest with a wrench in the pocket."
        height="200px"
      />
      <div class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Find me</p>
        <div class="links">
          <a href={SOCIAL.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener">&rarr; GitHub</a>
          <a href={SOCIAL.email}>&rarr; Mail</a>
          <a href="/rss.xml">&rarr; RSS</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .wrap { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 240px; gap: var(--space-7); padding-block: 34px 30px; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .wrap { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  h1 { margin: 0 0 16px; font: var(--type-title); letter-spacing: var(--type-display-track); max-width: 22ch; }
  p { margin: 0 0 14px; max-width: var(--measure-prose); font: var(--type-body); color: var(--ink-body); text-wrap: pretty; }

  .now {
    margin-top: 22px;
    max-width: var(--measure-prose);
    border: var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
    background: var(--violet-tint);
    padding: 16px 18px;
  }
  .now-label {
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    font: var(--type-eyebrow);
    letter-spacing: var(--type-eyebrow-track);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
  .now ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 20px; font: 400 15px/1.7 var(--font-body); color: var(--ink-body); }

  .side { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; }
  .card { border: var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-card); background: var(--surface); box-shadow: var(--shadow-card); padding: 14px 16px; }
  .eyebrow { margin: 0 0 10px; font: var(--type-tag); letter-spacing: var(--type-eyebrow-track); text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-subtle); }
  .links { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 7px; font: var(--type-toc); }
  .links a { color: var(--ink); text-decoration: none; }
</style>
